rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8380049Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8387595Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8457317Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8464987Z ^[[0m
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8465510Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8466203Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8466529Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8466795Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8467322Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8467571Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8467772Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8468177Z    if you are ready to continue.
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8468383Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8468789Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8469497Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8469906Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8470258Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8470419Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8470626Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8471079Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8471337Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8471707Z    can use Nix.
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8471863Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8471971Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8472186Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8472408Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8472858Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8482161Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8483128Z I will:
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8483633Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8484722Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8485410Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8485907Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8486444Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8486817Z  - install Nix in /nix
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8487173Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8487680Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8488201Z    /root
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8488637Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8489050Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8497944Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8498570Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8498830Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8501657Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8502612Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8514702Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8515734Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8522890Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8523383Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8523786Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8524292Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8524455Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8524702Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8524862Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8525211Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8525418Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8525537Z If you would like to
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8525877Z see the output, try like this:
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8526050Z 
rspec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-02T16:03:44.8526253Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
